Re-enable threaded NAPI on mtk_eth_soc.

pesa1234's RSS rework (999-2711, synced by 2b0188985c "sync MT7986 patches
from pesa1234 next-r4.9.0.rss.mtk") rewrote the dummy-device NAPI setup and
dropped the two lines that OpenWrt's generic pending-6.18/702 adds just
before the netif_napi_add() calls:

    eth->dummy_dev->threaded = 1;
    strcpy(eth->dummy_dev->name, "mtk_eth");

generic/pending-6.18/ is applied before target patches (include/quilt.mk), so
the net effect has been threaded NAPI silently disabled on mtk_eth_soc, with
the dummy netdev left named "dummy%d" -- hence no napi/mtk_eth-* kthreads.

dev->threaded is still a plain u8 in 6.18 (include/linux/netdevice.h) and
netif_napi_add_weight() still creates the kthread when it is set
(net/core/dev.c): the 6.18 dev_set_threaded() enum change is not involved
here, patch 702's direct write remains valid.

Setting the flag before the netif_napi_add_weight() calls covers tx_napi,
rx_napi[0] and every RSS ring in one go, exactly as 702 intended.

This must remain the last patch touching this block: 999-9910 is, as of now.

---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -6265,8 +6265,10 @@ static int mtk_probe(struct platform_dev
 		err = -ENOMEM;
 		dev_err(eth->dev, "failed to allocate dummy device\n");
 		goto err_deinit_ppe;
 	}
+	eth->dummy_dev->threaded = 1;
+	strcpy(eth->dummy_dev->name, "mtk_eth");
 	netif_napi_add_weight(eth->dummy_dev, &eth->tx_napi, mtk_napi_tx,
 			      MTK_NAPI_WEIGHT);
 	netif_napi_add_weight(eth->dummy_dev, &eth->rx_napi[0].napi, mtk_napi_rx,
 			      MTK_NAPI_WEIGHT);
